From: Adam Hillson <598804+BadAd84@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm cuda: pass the rows argument glm_tap_tests' prefillChunk lost in the port

tf-cuda-test failed to compile on pin+0001..0031 (found by the image build,
after 0032/0033): glm_tap_tests.zig:70 calls prefillChunk with the six-argument
form from before 0007 introduced the rows parameter; the engine takes
(part, start, rows, len, from, cancel, marks) - the same shape the engine's own
callers use (cuda_engine.zig:364, cuda_follow.zig:252). The test's loop already
computes rows two lines above, so the call passes it.

Gates: the image build glm53-zig:9c9bf54 (fatbins, install, native, sm_121a)
green on spark4, which compiles tf-cuda-test.
diff --git a/zig/tests/cuda/glm_tap_tests.zig b/zig/tests/cuda/glm_tap_tests.zig
--- a/zig/tests/cuda/glm_tap_tests.zig
+++ b/zig/tests/cuda/glm_tap_tests.zig
@@ -67,7 +67,7 @@
             while (true) : (at += C) {
                 const rows = @min(len - at, C);
                 const part = ids[at..@min(len, at + C + 1)];
-                const done = e.prefillChunk(part, at, len, null, null, null) catch |err| {
+                const done = e.prefillChunk(part, at, rows, len, null, null, null) catch |err| {
                     std.debug.print("FAIL tap: {s} prompt {d} chunk at {d}: {s}\n", .{ v.name, len, at, @errorName(err) });
                     return err;
                 };
